      "status": "complete",
      "text": "The key distinction is between retaining original matter and preserving an object through changes in matter. Repair can do the latter without doing the former. Burning the ship preserves a causal connection to its remains but not, ordinarily, the ship. And retaining every plank in a pile doesn’t by itself preserve an assembled vessel.",
      "annotations": [
